@description REAPER MCP — Model Context Protocol interface (immersive/spatial audio)
@version 1.13.2
@author James Livingston
@link https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_mcp.dylib https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet/releases/download/v$version/reaper_mcp.dylib
@changelog
  Documentation release: the standards basis now says WHICH loudness engine implements which
  revision of ITU-R BS.1770, and two public claims that were false are corrected. No functional change.

  `docs/CONVENTIONS.md` said "Standards basis throughout: ... ITU-R BS.1770-5". TWO loudness paths
  ship and they cite different revisions on purpose: REAPER's native RENDER_STATS program measure --
  `analysis.meter`'s program loudness and every deliverable-spec check -- is BS.1770-5, and the in-box
  C++ gated engine that measures stems, objects, the isolated dialog bus and folds that exist only in
  memory is BS.1770-4, pinned to it by unit test (Table 1's RLB numerator and Tables 4/5's channel
  weights). The word "throughout" was the only false statement. No engine changed and no measurement
  moves.

  `README.md` claimed CI builds the macOS / Windows / Linux matrix on every push. It does not: CI is
  Ubuntu-only on push, and the three-OS matrix runs on a version tag or a manual dispatch.

  `docs/MANUAL.md` hedged on the published ReaPack index URL. It now states it, and states the macOS
  signing posture plainly: the binary is ad-hoc codesigned -- the signature Apple Silicon requires to
  load it at all -- and is not notarized.

  Surface 190 tools / 4 resources / 5 prompts -- UNMOVED. ctest 28, unmoved.
